NNAAMMEE
     iissccssiidd — iSCSI (Internet SCSI) daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iissccssiidd [--ddvv] [--nn _d_e_v_i_c_e] [--ss _s_o_c_k_e_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     iissccssiidd is an Internet SCSI (iSCSI) initiator implementation.

     iissccssiidd is usually started at boot time.

     A running iissccssiidd can be controlled with the iscsictl(8) utility.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not daemonize.  If this option is specified, iissccssiidd will run
             in the foreground and log to _s_t_d_e_r_r.

     --nn _d_e_v_i_c_e
             Use an alternate /dev entry for communicating with the kernel.

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Use an alternate location for the default control socket.

     --vv      Produce more verbose output.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/iscsi.conf         Default iissccssiidd configuration file.
     /dev/vscsi0             Default device used to exchange SCSI messages
                             with the kernel midlayer.
     /var/run/iscsid.sock    UNIX-domain socket used for communication with
                             iscsictl(8).

